{{- /*
A write threading an open handle: the staging operation a mid-transaction
claim is stated about, drawn from the same pools the sequences write.

Bound from a method rather than supplied as a closure, and that is the whole
point. A supplied closure reaches past the interface to the concrete store —
`s.(*Impl).StageIt(...)` — and a defect worn on the interface then fails the
type assertion before the law observes anything, so no mutant can make the
claim false and it reads as bound but unsaturatable. An interface declaring a
claim about what its staging does has to declare the staging.
*/ -}}
{{- define "model.lawfield.HandleWrite" -}}
{{ .Name }}: func(rt *{{ renderExpr (external .ModelPkg "T") }}, s {{ renderType .Iface }}, h {{ renderType .In }}, k {{ renderType .Key }}, v {{ renderType .Value }}) error {
			return s.{{ .Method }}({{ if .TakesCtx }}rt.Context(), {{ end }}h, k, v)
		}
{{- end -}}
